      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it feels too intentional to be a coincidence. like, the scaling of the streets and the way the monuments intersect... it's exactly how a fractal antenna is supposed to be structured to capture certain wavelengths. if you treat the main axes as conductive paths and the parks as dielectric gaps, you could actually model this. can you try to run some rough math on it? like, if we assume the total area of the dc core is the aperture, what kind of frequency range would a structure shaped like that be tuned to? maybe we can see if it aligns with any specific stellar frequencies.",
